Z||000000||Old Lar||05-21-2001||02:50 PM||||The stock radio in my 88GT sounds like its on its wat out..the right channel is weak, and the right B pillar speaker pops and is really weak.  What are the chances its a loose connection or is the speaker shot?  The radio was "remanufactured" a couple of years ago. <P>Radio upgrade recommendations for a CD/AM-FM?<BR>I'm not looking for a 1000 watt amplifier system.  Just a good sounding radio CD player. I want one that fits into the Fiero radio cavity.<P>Front Fiero speakers were change to some Pioneer speakers that just dropped into place.<P>B Pillar speakers?||||reg||5
Z||000001||RossT||05-21-2001||03:00 PM||||Lar, I have two of these:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Gmplayer_3_1.jpg"> <P>both are out of 98 Grand Prix.  If you want I can bring one to the Dells Run for you to look at. It is plug and play with GM adapter<BR>part # 16140051 (I also can bring).  This unit will fit flush and has red light like the stock unit.  It also says "pontiac" on it. If you have the performance sound option you will need to cut one wire on the adapter and spice it to another.  I can show you. This unit also has the theftlock feature.  When activated it has a blinking red light that flashes when the car is off.  Kind of like an alarm system.  Aftermarket units like pioneer are also very nice, but in my opinion, don't look like they belong there. If your interested let me know.  I will sell it for what I paid for it.<P>Ross||||reg||1
Z||000002||ThatRickGuy||05-21-2001||03:17 PM||||Has anyone tryed using one of the new GP set ups w/ the stering wheel controls? <P>As far as your sterio is concerned, new speakers will make a huge difference.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Sootah||05-21-2001||03:25 PM||||If you want a good, cheap, CD player get the Pioneer DEH-1000. I have one and love it. The only thing that would make it nicer would be a remote for it, but that is only because I have it in my Cavalier (trying to sell it SOMEBODY buy it from me!!) and it has rear seats. In a fiero a remote wouldnt matter. Allthough they are cool. If you want sound quality get the Infinity Kappa component set. They still may be on sale in Crutchfield.<P>------------------<BR>Never argue with an idiot, they drag you down to their level and then beat you with experience||||reg||1
