Z||000011||stimpy||05-21-2001||10:54 PM||||Those GP units do look mighty slick. I do like my Pioneer DEH-P77-DH though. Great unit.  I got mine from <A HREF="http://www.competitionsound.com" TARGET=_blank>www.competitionsound.com</A> <BR>It has a lot of realy neat features, and it's pretty easy to use without looking at it.  Has built in alarm and comes with remote. But if you are not planning on adding any amps, then you'd prolly be happy with the Delco unit.||||reg||1
Z||000012||tgowens||05-21-2001||11:06 PM||||I have installed several of those Delco units with the equalizer and I really like the sound (I have them in all four of my GT's along with the stock sub-woofer system) and I have the one without the equalizer for my coupe. They are simple to install (plug and play unless you have the stock Performance Sound system.........then you need to splice two wires) and look great -- Larry, unless you want to spend more for an aftermarket unit, the "Pontiac" Delco unit is the way I would recommend (you may have seen the one in my gold GT in Louisville)........If you can't find one I can get you one as well as the adapter.......<P>------------------<BR>My Fiero Web Site.....<BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/index.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tgowens.gif">              </A><P>87 GT - 2.8L Gold automatic<BR>87 GT - 2.8L Blue automatic<BR>87 GT - 3.4L Blue 5-speed Getrag<BR>87 GT - 2.8L Med. Red Met. 5-speed Getrag<BR>88 Coupe - 2.5L Red automatic||||reg||1
